| 5 | U+2211 `∑` lexes as a prefix operator, never as an accumulator; only ASCII `SUM` is a big operator | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (parser) | `basic/expressions/reductions.tex`, "Summations and Other Reduction Expressions" (`Accumulator ::= Σ ∣ Π ∣ BIG (Encloser ∣ Op)`) | none | ours | `Operator prefix SUM is not defined.` The grammar's `Accumulator` takes the keyword `SUM`, which matches the ASCII letters only, and has no `∑` alternative (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/parser/Symbol.rats:252`, `:260-261`), so `∑` is read as a prefix operator. Fortify renders ASCII `SUM` as `Σ`, so the *rendered* form is unaffected. Workaround: write `SUM`. Probe `explorations/sum-probes/p13_unicode_sigma.fss`, in the parent of `e879b6a44`. |
| 81 | `label` / `exit` is unimplemented in the code generator | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (codegen) | `Specification-1.0-frozen/appendices/grammars/concrete-syntax.tex:972`, "Expressions" | none | ours | `Can't compile Label` (`CodeGen.sayWhat`). `CodeGen` declares no `forLabel` or `forExit`, so the node reaches `defaultCase`, which throws `sayWhat` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java:1674-1676`, `:1558-1561`). Workaround: write the loop without `exit`, as a `while` over a mutable flag. Probe `explorations/compiler-probes/p31.fss` (a `label L` round a `seq` loop that exits `with i`), in the parent of `c69cb2064`. full text: history, row 81 |
