| 322 | `atomic` as the trailing expression of a `do … also` arm produces a class that fails verification on the compiled path: `VerifyError: Inconsistent stackmap frames at branch target 5` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (codegen) | `Specification/basic/expressions/also.tex`, "Parallel Do Expressions"; `Specification/basic/expressions/atomic.tex`, "Atomic Expressions" | none | ours | siblings: 526. `CodeGen.generateTaskCompute` keeps `this` on the operand stack across the arm's body for the result's `PUTFIELD` (`CodeGen.java:5028-5036`); `CodeGen.forAtomicBlock` branches from its handler, which clears the stack, back to `startOver`, its first label (`:1736-1764`). So `atomic` is right only on an empty stack: not as an arm's trailing expression nor as a call's argument after the first. A `try … catch` in an arm fails the same way through `forTry` (`XXXTryInArmRungG`, with row 497). Walk is right. Workaround: put the `atomic` in a function the arm calls (`compiler_tests/AtomicTopLevelVar.fss`). probes and full text: history, row 322 |
| 324 | a Fortress exception thrown out of an `atomic` block leaves the block's writes visible on the compiled path: `atomic do g := 7; throw Boom end`, caught and read, gives 7 compiled and 100 under walk, at one thread and at four | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (codegen) | `Specification/basic/expressions/atomic.tex`, "Atomic Expressions" | none | ours | Also for a local and an object. Derived from code, not measured: `CodeGen.forAtomicBlock` handles only `TransactionAbortException` (`CodeGen.java:1742-1745`), so an `FException` leaves without `BaseTask.cleanupTransaction`, and `Transaction.TXRead` returns an ancestral write (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/runtimeSystem/Transaction.java:144-149,159-168`), which a later read finds; a second implicit thread reads it too (a child task takes its parent's transaction, `ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/runtimeSystem/BaseTask.java:83-86`). An `exit` to an enclosing `label` keeps the writes (`atomic.tex`). Workaround: throw after the block. probes and full text: history, row 324 |
| 526 | on the compiled path a `try` expression used as an operand or call argument after another value, `"a" \|\| (try f() catch e InvalidRange => "c" end)`, compiles and then fails verification at load, 'Inconsistent stackmap frames' | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (codegen) | `Specification-1.0-frozen/basic/expressions/try.tex:56-64`, "Try Expressions" | `ProjectFortress/compiler_tests/XXXTryOperandRungE.test` | climb batch 6.5b rung E's skeptic | siblings: 322. By reading, consistent with the verifier: `CodeGen.forTry` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java:2022`) emits the handler inline and the JVM clears the operand stack at a handler, so the value pushed before the `try` is gone on the `catch` path, which reaches the join with one value where the normal path has two. Also for a `try` that throws nothing; as the first operand it runs. Walk prints `ac`. Workaround: bind the `try` to a local first. Link test: `TryOperandRungELink.test`. full text: history, row 526 |
| 876 | the compiled `drandom` and `drandomZZ32` (`DeterministicRandom`) give values that depend on the schedule above one thread: a binary tree of tasks that draws at every node sums to a different value in each of three runs at `FORTRESS_THREADS=4` | CONTESTED | implementation gap (runtime) | silent | none | natives shared-state audit | A draw advances the current task's pedigree (`DeterministicRandom.java:52-56`, `ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/runtimeSystem/BaseTask.java:108-111`); a compiled `compute` sets the current task and never restores it (`CodeGen.java:5028-5033`), `joinOrRun` restores it only round a forked join (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/runtimeSystem/BaseTask.java:146-177`), at c124c6b65. `draws(12)` (`explorations/reviews/natives-shared-state-audit.md`, 3.2) printed 4111.755423548555, 4111.368862987949, 4110.961144549375. Contested: the specification is silent; the name and the pedigree comment promise it (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/runtimeSystem/BaseTask.java:57-61`). |
